            <ArticleTitle>Treating acute pain in the hospitalized patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-30; quiz 30-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000415872.67681.1e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many hospitalized patients report moderate-to-severe pain despite the use of epidural or patient-controlled analgesia. This article will explore the use of multimodal options for analgesia in hospitalized patients and focus on a difficult-to-treat acute pain condition, abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
